    <briefdescription>
<para>The CAN bootloader&apos;s wire contract (#363) — frame IDs, commands, replies, status codes, the entry flag and the protocol version. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>One source for every side of an update: the bootloader (Firmware/Bootloader), the running firmware that sends a node into it (<ref refid="namespaceSTM32Board" kindref="compound">STM32Board</ref> / <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol" kindref="compound">CANProtocol</ref>, #365), the bridge relay (<ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref>, #365), the Gateway uploader (#366) and the client sync. Header-only, no Arduino, no HAL — the bootloader builds bare-metal.</para>
<para>Every wire value is a named <computeroutput>enum class X : T { NAME = literal }</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>constexpr T NAME = literal</computeroutput> so the client sync can read it (#346). Full protocol: FirmwarePlan/12-bootloader.md.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="copyright"><para>GPL-2.0-only — see Firmware/LICENSE </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
